# syntek-base only — this file is copier-excluded, so a generated project never receives it.
#
# A research note answers one question against primary sources and feeds one decision. Notes
# written while developing the TEMPLATE answer questions about syntek-base itself — its skill
# surface, its rule sources — and a generated project inherits neither the questions nor the
# decisions they settled. Shipping them puts this template's internal reasoning into every
# project built from it.
#
# A generated project's notes are committed and synced, and its ADRs and plans link back to
# them, which is what research/CONTEXT.md describes. That is why this rule must not travel.
#
# Note the attribution consequence, because it cuts the right way: with nothing under research/
# shipped, no verbatim quotation of an unlicensed upstream source is redistributed by this
# template at all. THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md states that position; README.md Section Influences carries
# each row's evidence in the row itself rather than pointing at a note that no longer ships.
#
# The documentation pair stays tracked so the folder ships documented and ready to use.
*

# This file must stay tracked or the rule vanishes on a fresh clone, and copier.yml
# can only exclude a file the template actually carries.
!.gitignore
!*/
!CONTEXT.md
!CLAUDE.md
